# PCB Acceptance Standards Overview: IPC / GJB / GB/T Three-System Comparison

> A practical reference for hardware engineers, quality engineers, and procurement teams to understand PCB acceptance standards across **IPC**, **GJB**, and **GB/T** systems.

---

## 📌 Introduction

PCB acceptance standards are the common "yardstick" for hardware design, manufacturing, and quality control. However, the standard landscape can be confusing because different systems are used in different industries and regions:

- **IPC**: Global industry baseline for PCB workmanship and performance.
- **GJB**: China military standard for high-reliability defense and aerospace applications.
- **GB/T**: Chinese recommended national standards for civilian PCB manufacturing.

This repository provides a structured comparison of these three systems, including classification levels, key technical metrics, and practical acceptance workflows.

---

## 🔹 IPC International Standard System

IPC standards are widely used in global electronics manufacturing, especially in North America, Europe, and the Asia-Pacific region. They are divided into two main categories:

| Standard Type | Core Documents | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Workmanship Acceptance | IPC-A-600 | Visual inspection and cosmetic acceptance |
| Performance Specification | IPC-6010 series | Electrical, mechanical, and reliability requirements |
| Rigid PCB | IPC-6012 | Most commonly used for rigid PCBs |
| Flexible PCB | IPC-6013 | Flexible and rigid-flex PCBs |
| HDI PCB | IPC-6016 | High-density interconnect boards |
| High-Frequency PCB | IPC-6018 | Microwave and high-frequency boards |
| Test Methods | IPC-TM-650 | Standard test procedures |

### IPC Classification

| Class | Application | Reliability Requirement | Defect Tolerance |
|---|---|---|---|
| Class 1 | Consumer electronics, toys, appliances | Basic functionality | Cosmetic defects allowed |
| Class 2 | Industrial control, telecom, commercial automotive | Sustained performance | Minor defects allowed if not functional |
| Class 3 | Aerospace, medical devices, critical automotive hardware | High reliability, continuous operation | Near-zero defect tolerance |

> **Note:**  
> IPC-6012DS 3A, sometimes referred to as "Class 4", is an even higher level for space-grade avionics and military applications. It requires near-perfect manufacturing and is typically associated with higher cost.

### Key IPC Metrics

| Metric | Class 1 | Class 2 | Class 3 |
|---|---|---|---|
| Barrel Copper Thickness | No specific requirement | ≥ 20 μm average, ≥ 16 μm single point | ≥ 25 μm average, ≥ 20 μm single point |
| Outer Layer Copper | No requirement | ≥ 30 μm | ≥ 30 μm, strictly controlled |
| Annular Ring Width | No requirement | ≥ 50 μm | ≥ 50 μm, no breakout |
| Insulation Resistance | ≥ 100 MΩ | ≥ 500 MΩ | ≥ 1000 MΩ |
| Thermal Stress Test | 288°C / 10 s × 1 cycle | 288°C / 10 s × 3 cycles | 288°C / 10 s ≥ 3 cycles |
| Inspection Method | AQL sampling | AQL sampling, critical dimension inspection | 100% electrical test + full critical dimension inspection |

