## 🔹 GJB China National Military Standard System

GJB is the Chinese military standard system, primarily applied to defense, aerospace, and high-reliability electronic products. In the PCB field, GJB standards set stricter requirements for environmental resistance, traceability, and long-term reliability.

### Core GJB Standards

| Standard No. | Name | Application |
|---|---|---|
| GJB 362B-2009 | General Specification for Rigid Printed Boards | Main military PCB specification |
| GJB 5432-2005 | High-Reliability Soldering Requirements | Military assembly soldering processes |
| GJB 1032-2020 | Environmental Stress Screening | Temperature cycling and vibration shock |
| GJB 548C-2021 | Test Methods for Microelectronic Devices | IC and component reliability testing |

### GJB Grade Mapping

| GJB Grade | Approximate IPC Equivalent | Typical Application | Service Life |
|---|---|---|---|
| Grade Ⅰ | IPC Class 1 | General-purpose products | 5–10 years |
| Grade Ⅱ | IPC Class 2 | Industrial control, telecom equipment | Over 10 years |
| Grade Ⅲ | IPC Class 3+ | Military, aerospace, life support | Over 15 years |

> **Important:**  
> GJB Grade Ⅲ is generally stricter than IPC Class 3, especially in terms of environmental adaptability, traceability, and documentation requirements.

### Key GJB Requirements

| Metric | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Substrate Tg | ≥ 170°C |
| Barrel Copper Thickness | ≥ 25 μm |
| Dielectric Withstanding Voltage | ≥ 1000 V/mm |
| Ionic Contamination | ≤ 1.56 μg/cm² (NaCl equivalent) |
| Solder Mask Solvent Resistance | Required |
| Traceability | Full-process traceability |
| Quality System | GJB 9001 certification |

### Typical GJB Additional Tests

- Salt spray testing
- Solvent resistance testing
- Damp-heat cycling
- Vibration and shock testing
- Thermal shock testing from -55°C to +125°C
- Insulation resistance testing after damp heat
- Electromigration testing

