## 🔹 GB/T Chinese Recommended National Standards

GB/T standards are the national recommended standards in China. They are often used for civilian PCB manufacturing and can reference IEC and IPC standards.

Unlike IPC, GB/T does not use a universal Class 1/2/3 reliability grading system. Instead, PCB requirements are usually defined by board type:

- Single-sided PCBs
- Double-sided PCBs
- Multilayer PCBs
- Flexible PCBs

### Core GB/T Standards

| Standard No. | Description |
|---|---|
| GB/T 4588.1-1996 | Single/double-sided PCBs without PTH |
| GB/T 4588.2-1996 | Single/double-sided PCBs with PTH |
| GB/T 4588.3-2002 | PCB design and usage guide |
| GB/T 4588.4-2017 | Multilayer PCB performance requirements |
| GB/T 4677 series | PCB test methods |
| GB/T 4721–4725 series | Copper-clad laminate standards |

> **Update:**  
> GB/T 4588.1-1996 and GB/T 4588.2-1996 were withdrawn in July 2026 and replaced by **GB/T 4588-2025**.

### General Acceptance Level

GB/T acceptance requirements are generally comparable to **IPC Class 1 to Class 2**. For high-reliability or military projects, IPC or GJB standards are usually more appropriate.

